'' A LAMBDA IS AN ORDINARY PROCEDURE WITH A GENERATED NAME, and the expression is its
'' ADDRESS. Measured: fbc emits a function called L2B9C516C192D043_LT_0003 and writes
'' 'LESS$1 = (tmp$2)&L2B9C516C192D043_LT_0003'.
''
'' Nothing outside the module can name it, so the spelling is ours -- but it must not
'' COLLIDE across translation units, which is what the file's content hash is for: the
'' same job fbc's own hex prefix does.
''
'' HOISTED to module level rather than lowered in place, because a procedure is not an
'' expression: Collect declares it, Resolve binds its body, and the site that wrote it
'' gets '@name'. FreeBASIC lambdas CAPTURE NOTHING -- the body may name an enclosing
'' local's TYPE but not its value, and fbc rejects the latter with error 42 -- so
'' there is no closure to build.
''
'' THE PROBE THAT RECOGNISES ONE has to read the WHOLE signature: 'byref as long' is
'' part of it, and the one-line form ends in a COLON rather than an EOL. Missing
'' either made the body parse as statements where an expression belonged.
''
'' Beside it, A CALL THROUGH A PROCEDURE POINTER IS THE PROCEDURE'S RESULT TYPE. The
'' callee is a VARIABLE, so the overload machinery had nothing to score and the
'' expression came out untyped -- which is why 'print f( 1 )' declined while
'' 'dim as long v = f( 1 )' beside it lowered.
''
'' generics/lambda.bas: 17 -> 5.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/lambda.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: func.addr ptr __TKO_LAMBDA
'' GOLDEN: expected/lambda.out
